From 4348229dc58408e141c8814dab52dc0b4bcf94df Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 07:42:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban placement: a pool worker's
 home-gateway-marker hit joins the pool queue unless it holds the card's state

On a Linux pool worker (the t_01a1d2662553185d gateway test: readable Board registry entry, `linux`, not the hub,
a live pool label), a home-gateway-marker hit no longer keeps a card on its creating worker by itself. Each hit is
classified (HOME_MARKER_CLASSES):

- worktree path: kept only when a named root exists here and is dirty or has unpushed commits
  (kanban_move_pool.tree_state(refresh=False, remote_timeout<=5): ls-remote only, <=5 trees in one 5 s budget,
  errors/timeouts/non-git roots keep); otherwise queues with no extra label.
- state path: kept only when a named ~/.hermes/kanban/{workspaces,evidence,attachments}/<x> or cache/scratch/<x>
  exists here; any other state path queues with capability:hub-write.
- 'this host' and operator extra_home_markers: kept.
- (b) hub/fleet (hermes-sync, on the hub, kanban.db, cron, systemctl, ...): queue + capability:hub-write.
- (c) launchd: queue + capability:tailnet-exec. (d) ssh, token-broker: queue.

Any keep hit keeps the card (why prefix "home gateway marker:" unchanged, plus a note naming what this worker
holds); otherwise runs_on = [pool label, *sorted(class labels | coordination labels | sibling local-group labels)],
with QUEUED_WHY + " (home gateway marker <hit> not bound to <gateway>)" and a per-class note. As for local markers
(cfc3d681ce), the queue happens only when one live machine holds the whole label set; otherwise the local keep
stands and the audit records gateway-test-failed. The created event
gets an optional `home_marker` {decision, class, hit} record (also `gateway-test-failed` when a non-hub worker
could not test its gateway). portability() stays probe-free (new home_markers=False flag); the published-worktree
exemption still runs first. All three front doors (tool, CLI, direct create) share the decision.

Reverses one assertion: t_01a1d2662553185d's control "systemctl restart x on w2 -> unchanged" now expects
[pool:worker, capability:hub-write] (spec case (c)). The pool-worker fixture now carries the live label set
(hub-write, tailnet-exec, token-broker), so cfc3d681ce's _no_live_tailnet_pool_worker strips tailnet-exec
explicitly to keep its premise; its assertions are unchanged.

Proof: RED 19 failed / 62 passed on base 141bcec62a (new pool_queue cases); after the rebase onto 87b1e0cbbe the
unclaimable-audit case was RED first too. Head (tree a705d72040): 27 placement/move/worker/hub-admission files
1397 passed (base 87b1e0cbbe 1365; pool_queue +31, published_worktree +1, others unchanged); 27 mutants incl. the
six spec mutations, all killed; scripts/check 19 ok.

Card: t_01a1d2856e5fec44 (spec t_01a1d27970ab4bca).
